      "original": "Printed normalized Gibbs mu, true R_eta,y with quadratic denominator2eta, actual proximal p, Ex8 residual rho and true standardized affine law r; authored canonical-entropy/coherence component sets gamma=N(0,I), Z=∫exp(-rho)gamma,q=exp(-rho)/Z, actual canonical ENNReal KL and canonical RN llr.",
      "reconstructed": "A potential V:E→ℝ, condition parameter κ, measurable parameter functions η:S→ℝ and y:S→E, and an internally produced measurable stationary solution p:S→E. Define ρ_s(u)=V(p_s+√η_s u)−V(p_s)−√η_s⟨∇V(p_s),u⟩; μ=volume tilted by −V; R_s=μ tilted by −‖x−y_s‖²/(2η_s); r_s is the pushforward of R_s by x↦(√η_s)⁻¹(x−p_s); γ is the centered covariance-identity Gaussian; Z_s=∫exp(−ρ_s)dγ and q_s(u)=exp(−ρ_s(u))/Z_s. Tilts are normalized exponential tilts when integrable, and zero measures otherwise.",
