      "reconstructed": "For every such E and S, every V and κ satisfying the global hypotheses, and every measurable η and y with η(s)>0 for every s, there exists one measurable function p. For every s, p_s solves p_s+η_s∇V(p_s)=y_s; for every s and every z∈E satisfying z+η_s∇V(z)=y_s, z=p_s. The same p defines every downstream measure and function, and all subsequent conclusions hold for every s.",
