      "reconstructed": "All stationary equations, Hessian bounds and witness uniqueness statements are pointwise in their displayed variables. The likelihood-representative equality is only almost everywhere under r_s, not a pointwise identity or an equality only under γ. The relative-entropy finiteness is an explicit extended-real claim, distinct from its real-valued .toReal identities. Both entropy identities use the same literal r_s, γ, ρ_s and Z_s produced from the same p. The pushforward is the actual measure map, and integrability is genuine Bochner integrability.",
